This based PR https://github.com/goplus/gop/pull/628
* support interface type and compatible Go interface
* support type assert expr
* support type switch stmt

Go+ code
```
package main

import (
	"bytes"
	"fmt"
)

type B interface {
	WriteString(s string) (n int, err error)
}

type T interface {
	B
	String() string
}

func main() {
	b := new(bytes.Buffer)
	b.WriteString("hello")
	var t T = b
	t.WriteString(" world")

	switch v := t.(type) {
	case fmt.Stringer:
		fmt.Println(v)
	default:
		fmt.Printf("unknown type %T\n",v)
	}
}
```
generate Golang code
```
package main

import (
	bytes "bytes"
	fmt "fmt"
)

type (
	B interface {
		WriteString(string) (int, error)
	}
	T interface {
		String() string
		WriteString(string) (int, error)
	}
)

func main() {
	var (
		b *bytes.Buffer
		t T
	)
//line ./main.gop:19
	b = new(bytes.Buffer)
//line ./main.gop:20
	(*bytes.Buffer).WriteString(b, "hello")
//line ./main.gop:21
	t = b
//line ./main.gop:22
	(T).WriteString(t, " world")
	{
		var _q_gop_v T
		_q_gop_v = t
		_ = _q_gop_v
		{
			var (
				ok bool
				v  fmt.Stringer
			)
//line ./main.gop:24
			v, ok = _q_gop_v.(fmt.Stringer)
//line ./main.gop:25
			if !ok {
				goto _gop_1
			}
			_ = v
			{
//line ./main.gop:26
				fmt.Println(v)
			}
//line ./main.gop:25
			goto _gop_2
//line ./main.gop:25
			goto _gop_1
		_gop_1:
			{
				var v T
//line ./main.gop:24
				v = _q_gop_v
				_ = v
				{
//line ./main.gop:28
					fmt.Printf("unknown type %T\n", v)
				}
			}
//line ./main.gop:25
			goto _gop_2
		_gop_2:
		}
	}
}
```

This PR is to add a post-submit job to build and test `etcd-io/etcd` for every commit in master golang code upstream.
This is to move Jenkins job https://github.ibm.com/powercloud/test-infra/blob/master/jobs/pipelines/test-etcd-master/Jenkinsfile to Prow.
We are not using any specific image like https://github.ibm.com/powercloud/test-infra/blob/master/images/etcd-test/Dockerfile for this prow job as `all-in-one` image available in `quay.io/powercloud `is taking care of basic dependencies needed. _(like curl, make, git etc.)_

Even without installing additional dependencies from https://github.ibm.com/powercloud/test-infra/blob/master/images/etcd-test/Dockerfile#L67:L77, We are able to build and test etcd successfully!

